<com:TContent ID="body" >

<h1>TTable</h1>
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.WebControls.TTable" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TTable</tt> displays an HTML table on a page. It is used together with <tt>TTableRow</tt> and <tt>TTableCell</tt> to allow programmatically manipulating HTML tables. The rows of the table is stored in <tt>Rows</tt> property. The table caption can be specified via <tt>Caption</tt> whose alignment is specified by <tt>CaptionAlign</tt>, and <tt>BackImageUrl</tt> gives the table a background image.
</p>

<h2>Presentational properties to avoid</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Three properties write HTML attributes that HTML5 dropped, and the framework marks all
three deprecated. They still render, so existing pages keep working. CSS replaces each of
them, through the <tt>Style</tt> property or a class named by <tt>CssClass</tt>.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Deprecated property</th><th>Writes</th><th>Use instead</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>CellSpacing</tt></td>
	<td><tt>cellspacing</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>border-spacing</tt> declaration.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>CellPadding</tt></td>
	<td><tt>cellpadding</tt></td>
	<td>The CSS <tt>border-collapse</tt> declaration set to <tt>collapse</tt>, with <tt>padding</tt> on the cells.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>GridLines</tt></td>
	<td><tt>border</tt></td>
	<td>CSS borders on the individual elements.</td>
</tr>
</table>
<h2>Table sections</h2>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.0.1" />

<p class="block-content">
A row states which part of the table it belongs to. <tt>TTableRow</tt> carries a
<tt>TableSection</tt> property that takes <tt>Header</tt>, <tt>Body</tt>, or
<tt>Footer</tt>, and defaults to <tt>Body</tt>. <tt>TTable</tt> groups consecutive rows of
the same section into a <tt>&lt;thead&gt;</tt>, a <tt>&lt;tbody&gt;</tt>, or a
<tt>&lt;tfoot&gt;</tt> element.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Two subclasses fix the section instead of leaving it to a property.
<tt>TTableHeaderRow</tt> always reports <tt>Header</tt>, and <tt>TTableFooterRow</tt>
always reports <tt>Footer</tt>. Assigning <tt>TableSection</tt> on either one raises a
<tt>TInvalidOperationException</tt>.
</p>

<com:TTextHighlighter CssClass="source block-content">
&lt;com:TTable&gt;
  &lt;com:TTableHeaderRow&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableHeaderCell Scope="Column"&gt;Product&lt;/com:TTableHeaderCell&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableHeaderCell Scope="Column"&gt;Units&lt;/com:TTableHeaderCell&gt;
  &lt;/com:TTableHeaderRow&gt;
  &lt;com:TTableRow&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableCell&gt;Widget&lt;/com:TTableCell&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableCell&gt;120&lt;/com:TTableCell&gt;
  &lt;/com:TTableRow&gt;
  &lt;com:TTableFooterRow&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableCell&gt;Total&lt;/com:TTableCell&gt;
    &lt;com:TTableCell&gt;120&lt;/com:TTableCell&gt;
  &lt;/com:TTableFooterRow&gt;
&lt;/com:TTable&gt;
</com:TTextHighlighter>

<h2>Header cells</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TTableHeaderCell</tt> renders a <tt>&lt;th&gt;</tt> element and adds three properties
that describe the cell to assistive technology.
</p>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Renders</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Scope</tt></td>
	<td><tt>scope</tt></td>
	<td>States what the header labels. It takes <tt>Row</tt>, <tt>Column</tt>, or <tt>NotSet</tt>.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>AbbreviatedText</tt></td>
	<td><tt>abbr</tt></td>
	<td>A short form of the header text.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>CategoryText</tt></td>
	<td><tt>axis</tt></td>
	<td>A comma separated list of categories the cell belongs to. Deprecated, because HTML5 dropped the attribute. Use <tt>Scope</tt>.</td>
</tr>
</table>

